@@coopmoe output {"cell": "indep_cat_box1", "id": "finance-0002", "category": "finance", "box": 1, "prompt_tokens": 20, "output_tokens": 128, "ttft_s": 3.3841, "tpot_ms": 396.7, "e2e_s": 53.7693, "wait_s": 187.8665, "measured": true, "request": "Why does the Brexit cause a fall in crude oil prices?", "output": "Brexit itself does not directly cause a fall in crude oil prices, but it can indirectly influence oil prices through its impact on global economic conditions, trade, and market sentiment. Here’s how Brexit could contribute to lower crude oil prices:\n\n### 1. **Weakening of the UK and European Economy**\n- Brexit, especially a disorderly or prolonged exit, can create economic uncertainty in the UK and the broader European Union.\n- Reduced economic growth in Europe (a major oil consumer) leads to lower demand for crude oil.\n- Lower demand → downward pressure on oil prices.\n\n### 2. **Weaker Pound Sterling (GBP)**\n"}
